## Program Definition (static, hard-coded)

All 4 days fully specified with:
- Exercise name, sets, reps, unit (dumbbell / plates / bodyweight), muscle group, difficulty
- Warmup routine (4 items per day, day-specific)
- Coaching notes per exercise
- Swap catalog: alternate exercises keyed by muscle group
- Tutorial text per exercise
- Exercise IDs: ua1–ua6, la1–la6, ub1–ub7, lb1–lb6

> **Superseded by the program-unlock (un-hardlock) work:** the program is now data-driven + auto-generated from `ExerciseLibrary` (a single equipment-tagged pool of 52 movements with per-exercise coaching rationale). The old `Swaps` catalog was merged into the library, so the **swap picker and the generator now draw from the same pool**, filtered by available equipment + dislikes.
>
> **"Professional plans" engine (all 6 phases complete):** the generator is goal-aware (rep ranges), experience-aware (volume scale + difficulty cap), frequency-aware (weekly volume via `VolumeModel`), role/pattern-aware (heavy slots → bilateral compounds, no duplicate movement patterns), and safety-aware (problem-area avoidance). Tunable from **Settings → Program**: days/week, goal, experience, priority muscles, problem areas, cadence, deload week, + a **live per-muscle weekly-volume readout**; per-exercise ♥/✕/📌 (like/dislike/pin) on the Exercise-likes page; single-day re-roll from the day-card long-press menu. Onboarding (10 steps) collects all inputs and shows a **live sample-week preview** before finishing. Rest-timer durations + day-card "~min" estimates come from `SessionEstimate`. See `.claude/program-unlock-plan.md`.

