## UI / Design System

- Material 3, dark theme (Pearl), custom color palette
- Per-day accent colors extracted from hex strings (toAccentColor())
- bounceClick modifier: spring-animated scale (0.97×) on press, no ripple (scale is the affordance)
- Radial bloom gradients via Modifier.drawBehind (smooth fade, no hard edges)
- Linear gradients on NavTiles (primary: accent 0.28→0.10, secondary: surface→accent 0.08)
- Typography: Display / Headline / Title / Body / Label hierarchy applied consistently
- ModalBottomSheet for log sheets and session summary
- AlertDialog for destructive confirmations

### Editorial Redesign (v0.3)

The editorial pass simplified Overview + Stats + Trophies to no-card hairline layouts. Many feature cards documented elsewhere in this file were stripped from their screens during this pass — see "🔒 Audit" near the top.

- **Pearl dark theme**: gradient bg `#131318` → `#090909` applied at root in `ForgeTheme`; Indigo light defined but not wired
- **Typography**: `headlineLarge/Medium/Small` = `FontFamily.Serif Normal`; `labelLarge/Medium/Small` = `FontFamily.Monospace`; body = SansSerif
- **Gradient show-through**: all Scaffolds + TopAppBars set `containerColor = Color.Transparent`; root `ForgeTheme` wraps content in gradient `Box`
- **No-card editorial style**: `HorizontalDivider(alpha 0.3f)` hairlines instead of Surface cards on Overview
- **Accent color presets**: 4 options (Navy #3D4F73 default, Red #8B3535, Olive #4D6040, Gold #7A6435) — user-selectable in Settings, persisted to DataStore via `SettingsRepository.accentColorHex`, wired through `ForgeUiSettings` → `ForgeTheme` → `primary` token
- **OverviewScreen**: see "Overview Screen" section above for the precise current layout. Note: the originally-planned dynamic hero (comeback / streak text) and inline OnThisDay are no longer present — only the day name renders.
- **WarmupGate**: removed Surface card wrapper — plain Column with monospace `WARMUP` label
- **TrophiesScreen**: serif "N of 21." hero count + `LinearProgressIndicator(height = 2.dp)` — no card wrapper
- **SettingsScreen**: accent color `FilterChip` row in Appearance section (Navy / Red / Olive / Gold)

